  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "All L1 gold records report absolute or systemic bioavailability values or qualitative outcomes at or above about 35% (rigosertib 35%/34.8%, GDC-0810 ~45%, alfuzosin 49%, colchicine 44-55%, midodrine 90-100%, indomethacin 76-80%, omeprazole ~100%, 5-HTP 49%, loratadine good), so the gold evidence direction uniformly supports F >= 20%.",
      "card_ids": [
        "C01","C02","C03","C04","C05","C06","C07","C08","C09","C10",
        "C11","C12","C13","C14","C15","C16","C17","C18","C19","C20","C21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 records reinforce the same direction: alfuzosin ~49% fed, rigosertib 35 ± 18%, GDC-0810 40-60%, indomethacin ~93-102% in rabbits, colchicine ~25-50%, midodrine >90%, omeprazole 98%, 5-HTP 40%, and loratadine 40%; none reports F < 20%.",
      "card_ids": [
        "C22","C23","C24","C25","C26","C27","C28","C29","C30",
        "C31","C32","C33","C34","C35","C36","C37","C38","C39","C40"
      ]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The most structurally relevant contexts—alfuzosin (diaminopyrimidine/quinazoline, dimethoxy, amide) and the large polar/lipophilic rigosertib and GDC-0810—support F values of 35-60%, above the 20% threshold despite high molecular weight and TPSA.",
      "card_ids": ["C01","C18","C07","C10","C12","C32","C33","C36"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The low physicochemical prior (high MW, TPSA, logP/logD, low Fsp3) is not affirmative endpoint evidence for F < 20%; no transferable record reports F below 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C07","C10","C12","C32"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The L3 oral Cmax/AUC records for heptamethoxyflavone, nobiletin, melatonin, and an imidafenacin metabolite are pg/mL-level exposures without IV comparators or F values and are not structurally aligned with the query; they neither support nor contradict the F >= 20% decision.",
      "card_ids": [
        "C41","C42","C43","C44","C45","C46","C47","C48","C49","C50","C51","C52"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": [
        "C41","C42","C43","C44","C45","C46","C47","C48","C49","C50","C51","C52"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct query-specific absolute oral bioavailability measurement is available; the decision relies on cross-molecule transfer.",
    "L3 records report only Cmax or AUC without IV comparators or F values, so they cannot quantify bioavailability.",
    "No L1/L2/L3 record reports F < 20% for a molecule with comparable size and polarity; a low prediction would rest on the physicochemical prior alone.",
    "The query has no reported external condition, limiting direct transfer of condition-specific contexts such as fasted, fed, modified-release, or cirrhosis.",
    "High TPSA, high logP/logD, high molecular weight, and low Fsp3 may reduce absorption or solubility, but no transferable low-F record quantifies this effect.",
    "Some L2 records are qualitative, relative, or animal data with high variability and small sample sizes; they are context rather than independent gold votes."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L3 adds only oral Cmax/AUC records for unrelated molecules without F values or IV comparators; they are neutral and do not alter the decision. All L1 gold records and L2 context support F >= 20%, with no transferable record below 20%. Prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

